# Remote Media Download

Remote URLs (YouTube, Instagram, X/Twitter, and other yt-dlp sites) are handled by [`src/remote/`](mdc:src/remote/index.ts).

## Module layout

- **providers.ts** — site registry (`youtube`, `instagram`, `generic`): match, normalize, slug, `needsCookies`
- **urls.ts** — `isRemoteMediaUrl`, `normalizeRemoteMediaUrl`, `getRemoteMediaSlug`
- **ytdlp.ts** — `probeInfo` / `extractAudio` process wrappers
- **cookies.ts** — `--cookies-from-browser` resolution (Instagram)
- **progress.ts** — percent bar or live spinner
- **index.ts** — `downloadRemoteAudio` orchestration

## URL Detection

```typescript
import { isRemoteMediaUrl, isYouTubeUrl, isInstagramUrl } from './remote'

isYouTubeUrl('https://youtu.be/VIDEO_ID')
isInstagramUrl('https://www.instagram.com/reel/SHORTCODE/')
isRemoteMediaUrl('https://x.com/user/status/123') // generic http(s)
```

YouTube supports watch, Shorts, and youtu.be (with or without `https://`).
Instagram supports `/reel/`, `/reels/`, `/p/`, `/tv/`.

## Download Strategy

Always extract audio-only via yt-dlp (`-x --audio-format mp3`) into the system temp directory. Clean up the downloaded file in a `finally` block after transcription.

Instagram (and other `needsCookies` providers) auto-detect browser cookies. Override with `--cookies-from-browser chrome`.

## Adding a site

Add a `RemoteProvider` in `providers.ts` (before `generic`). Prefer that over branching inside `downloadRemoteAudio`.

## Progress UX

- Known filesize → percent bar
- Unknown size (HLS, etc.) → live spinner with bytes/speed
